/* Verse Games: THE WHOLE COUNSEL · Numbers chapters 21-25
   Verse text is filled/verified from the KJV by tools/fill-verses.js */
VG.registerBibleChapters("numbers", [
{n:21, name:"The Bronze Serpent", seal:{ref:"Numbers 21:9",verse:"And Moses made a serpent of brass, and put it upon a pole, and it came to pass, that if a serpent had bitten any man, when he beheld the serpent of brass, he lived."}, facts:["Did you know Jesus Himself pointed back to this chapter, saying, \"And as Moses lifted up the serpent in the wilderness, even so must the Son of man be lifted up\" (John 3:14)?","Did you know Israel later worshipped the bronze serpent itself, calling it Nehushtan, until King Hezekiah broke it in pieces (2 Kings 18:4)?","Did you know the king's highway that Israel asked Sihon to use was an ancient trade road running through the Transjordan, and Sihon's refusal to open it cost him his kingdom?"], questions:[
{q:"Which king attacked Israel as they came up by the way of the spies?", options:["King Arad the Canaanite, which dwelt in the south","Sihon king of the Amorites","Og king of Bashan","Balak the son of Zippor"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 21:1",verse:"And when king Arad the Canaanite, which dwelt in the south, heard tell that Israel came by the way of the spies; then he fought against Israel, and took some of them prisoners.", insight:"Trouble came from the south before the victories did; God often lets us face Arad before He gives us Sihon."},
{q:"What did Israel vow unto the LORD after Arad took prisoners?", options:["If thou wilt deliver this people into my hand, then I will utterly destroy their cities","They would never fight again","They would return to Egypt","They would build an altar at Hormah"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 21:2",verse:"And Israel vowed a vow unto the LORD, and said, If thou wilt indeed deliver this people into my hand, then I will utterly destroy their cities.", insight:"A vow born of trouble is still heard; God honors the bargains His people make in fear."},
{q:"What did Israel call the place where the LORD delivered the Canaanites?", options:["Hormah","Beer","Heshbon","Ijeabarim"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 21:3",verse:"And the LORD hearkened to the voice of Israel, and delivered up the Canaanites; and they utterly destroyed them and their cities: and he called the name of the place Hormah.", insight:"They named the place of victory Hormah, utter destruction; remember where God fought for you by name."},
{q:"What route did Israel take from mount Hor?", options:["By the way of the Red sea, to compass the land of Edom","Straight through the land of Edom","Across the Jordan into Canaan","Back toward mount Sinai"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 21:4",verse:"And they journeyed from mount Hor by the way of the Red sea, to compass the land of Edom: and the soul of the people was much discouraged because of the way.", insight:"A long way around Edom discouraged their souls; detours test faith even when obedience requires them."},
{q:"What did the people complain about in the wilderness?", options:["There is no bread, neither is there any water, and their soul loathed the light bread","The water was bitter and the tents were torn","Moses had taken all the gold","The Amorites had stolen their flocks"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 21:5",verse:"And the people spake against God, and against Moses, Wherefore have ye brought us up out of Egypt to die in the wilderness? for there is no bread, neither is there any water; and our soul loatheth this light bread.", insight:"They loathed the light bread, the very provision of heaven; grumbling calls God's gifts contemptible."},
{q:"What judgment did the LORD send among the murmuring people?", options:["Fiery serpents, and they bit the people","A plague of frogs","Hail from heaven","A famine of three years"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 21:6",verse:"And the LORD sent fiery serpents among the people, and they bit the people; and much people of Israel died.", insight:"Fiery serpents bit the complainers; sometimes the cure for a bitter mouth is a sharp one."},
{q:"What did the people ask Moses to do about the serpents?", options:["Pray unto the LORD, that he take away the serpents from us","Lead them back to Egypt","Kill the serpents with swords","Build a wall against them"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 21:7",verse:"Therefore the people came to Moses, and said, We have sinned, for we have spoken against the LORD, and against thee; pray unto the LORD, that he take away the serpents from us. And Moses prayed for the people.", insight:"They confessed, 'We have sinned'; confession is the doorway back to mercy."},
{q:"What remedy did the LORD command Moses to make?", options:["A fiery serpent, set upon a pole","An altar of brass at the camp gate","A brazen laver for washing","A banner of blue cloth"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 21:8",verse:"And the LORD said unto Moses, Make thee a fiery serpent, and set it upon a pole: and it shall come to pass, that every one that is bitten, when he looketh upon it, shall live.", insight:"Look and live; salvation by looking is the whole gospel in miniature."},
{q:"When did the bitten live?", options:["When he beheld the serpent of brass","When he reached the land of Canaan","When Moses prayed over him by name","When the plague had run its course"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 21:9",verse:"And Moses made a serpent of brass, and put it upon a pole, and it came to pass, that if a serpent had bitten any man, when he beheld the serpent of brass, he lived.", insight:"One look at the lifted serpent, and he lived; faith needs no ladder, only a lifted eye."},
{q:"Where did Israel pitch after leaving Oboth?", options:["At Ijeabarim, in the wilderness before Moab, toward the sunrising","At mount Hor","In the valley of Eshcol","At the brooks of Arnon"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 21:11",verse:"And they journeyed from Oboth, and pitched at Ije-abarim, in the wilderness which is before Moab, toward the sunrising.", insight:"Camp by camp, God was leading them toward the sunrising; every night's rest is a step toward morning."},
{q:"Which river marked the border of Moab where Israel pitched?", options:["Arnon, the border between Moab and the Amorites","Jabbok","Jordan","Jabbok and Jordan together"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 21:13",verse:"From thence they removed, and pitched on the other side of Arnon, which is in the wilderness that cometh out of the coasts of the Amorites: for Arnon is the border of Moab, between Moab and the Amorites.", insight:"God led them along borders He would soon redraw; the map changes when the promise arrives."},
{q:"What ancient book is quoted about the wars at Arnon?", options:["The book of the wars of the LORD","The book of the kings of Moab","The chronicles of the Amorites","The song of the Red sea"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 21:14",verse:"Wherefore it is said in the book of the wars of the LORD, What he did in the Red sea, and in the brooks of Arnon,", insight:"There is a book of the wars of the LORD; God keeps a record of every battle He fights for you."},
{q:"What is Beer?", options:["The well whereof the LORD said, Gather the people together, and I will give them water","The city of Sihon","The plain of Moab","The mountain of the Amorites"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 21:16",verse:"And from thence they went to Beer: that is the well whereof the LORD spake unto Moses, Gather the people together, and I will give them water.", insight:"Beer means well; God gives water where His people gather at His word."},
{q:"What song did Israel sing at Beer?", options:["Spring up, O well; sing ye unto it","The LORD is my strength and song","Who is like unto thee, O LORD","Bless the LORD, O my soul"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 21:17",verse:"Then Israel sang this song, Spring up, O well; sing ye unto it:", insight:"They sang to the well before they drank; praise that precedes provision is the song of faith."},
{q:"Who digged the well at Beer?", options:["The princes and nobles of the people, by the direction of the lawgiver, with their staves","Moses alone with his rod","The Levites with silver trumpets","The servants of Sihon"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 21:18",verse:"The princes digged the well, the nobles of the people digged it, by the direction of the lawgiver, with their staves. And from the wilderness they went to Mattanah:", insight:"Princes dug with staves; no work is beneath leaders when God's people are thirsty."},
{q:"To whom did Israel send messengers asking passage?", options:["Sihon king of the Amorites","Og king of Bashan","Balak king of Moab","The king of Edom"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 21:21",verse:"And Israel sent messengers unto Sihon king of the Amorites, saying,", insight:"Israel asked peaceably first; the gospel still comes with a request before it comes with a sword."},
{q:"What road did Israel ask to use through Sihon's land?", options:["The king's high way, until past his borders","The road through the vineyards","The path by the wells","The way of the spies"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 21:22",verse:"Let me pass through thy land: we will not turn into the fields, or into the vineyards; we will not drink of the waters of the well: but we will go along by the king’s high way, until we be past thy borders.", insight:"They promised to touch nothing, field, vineyard, or well; a righteous cause needs no plunder."},
{q:"How far did Israel possess Sihon's land?", options:["From Arnon unto Jabbok, even unto the children of Ammon","From Egypt unto the Red sea","From Heshbon unto mount Hor","From Moab unto the Jordan"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 21:24",verse:"And Israel smote him with the edge of the sword, and possessed his land from Arnon unto Jabbok, even unto the children of Ammon: for the border of the children of Ammon was strong.", insight:"From Arnon to Jabbok, God measured out the victory; He enlarges borders for obedient feet."},
{q:"What had Sihon done at Heshbon?", options:["Fought the former king of Moab, and taken all his land","Built the temple of Baal","Made a league with Og","Burned the fields of the Ammonites"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 21:26",verse:"For Heshbon was the city of Sihon the king of the Amorites, who had fought against the former king of Moab, and taken all his land out of his hand, even unto Arnon.", insight:"Sihon had taken Moab's land by war; the conqueror was about to be conquered."},
{q:"What happened to Og king of Bashan at Edrei?", options:["Israel smote him, and his sons, and all his people, until none was left alive, and possessed his land","He fled into the wilderness and was never found","He made peace and paid tribute","He joined Israel against Moab"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 21:35",verse:"So they smote him, and his sons, and all his people, until there was none left him alive: and they possessed his land.", insight:"None was left alive of Og's host; when God says fear not, the giant is already fallen."}
]},
{n:22, name:"Balak and Balaam", seal:{ref:"Numbers 22:12",verse:"And God said unto Balaam, Thou shalt not go with them; thou shalt not curse the people: for they are blessed."}, facts:["Did you know Balaam's donkey is the only animal in the Bible whose mouth the LORD Himself is said to have opened (Numbers 22:28)?","Did you know the apostle Peter later named Balaam's ruin plainly, calling him one who \"loved the wages of unrighteousness\" (2 Peter 2:15)?","Did you know Balak paid good silver for a curse and received four blessings instead, a bargain he never wanted?"], questions:[
{q:"What made Balak fear Israel?", options:["He saw all that Israel had done to the Amorites","Israel had crossed the Jordan","The spies had entered Jericho","Moses had died in Moab"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 22:2",verse:"And Balak the son of Zippor saw all that Israel had done to the Amorites.", insight:"Balak measured Israel by what they had done to the Amorites; men fear the works of God more than His words."},
{q:"How did Moab react to Israel's numbers?", options:["Moab was sore afraid, and distressed because of the children of Israel","Moab rejoiced and sent gifts","Moab ignored them entirely","Moab joined them in battle"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 22:3",verse:"And Moab was sore afraid of the people, because they were many: and Moab was distressed because of the children of Israel.", insight:"Sore afraid and distressed; the enemies of God's people often fear them before they ever fight them."},
{q:"How did the elders of Moab describe Israel's advance?", options:["This company shall lick up all that are round about us, as the ox licketh up the grass of the field","They shall pass over us as a river","They shall wither like grass in summer","They shall scatter as chaff"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 22:4",verse:"And Moab said unto the elders of Midian, Now shall this company lick up all that are round about us, as the ox licketh up the grass of the field. And Balak the son of Zippor was king of the Moabites at that time.", insight:"An ox licking up grass; fear paints God's people as a devouring beast."},
{q:"Where did Balaam the son of Beor live?", options:["Pethor, by the river of the land of the children of his people","In the plains of Moab","At mount Hor","In the city of Heshbon"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 22:5",verse:"He sent messengers therefore unto Balaam the son of Beor to Pethor, which is by the river of the land of the children of his people, to call him, saying, Behold, there is a people come out from Egypt: behold, they cover the face of the earth, and they abide over against me:", insight:"God fetched His prophet's mouth from Pethor by the river; He can call a witness from anywhere."},
{q:"What did Balak ask Balaam to do?", options:["Come, curse me this people, for they are too mighty for me","Bless Israel in the sight of Moab","Seduce Israel with the daughters of Midian","Build altars to Chemosh"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 22:6",verse:"Come now therefore, I pray thee, curse me this people; for they are too mighty for me: peradventure I shall prevail, that we may smite them, and that I may drive them out of the land: for I wot that he whom thou blessest is blessed, and he whom thou cursest is cursed.", insight:"'Curse me this people'; Balak wanted heaven's mouth to serve his fear."},
{q:"What reputation did Balaam carry?", options:["He whom thou blessest is blessed, and he whom thou cursest is cursed","He could call down fire from heaven","He had defeated the Amorites","He spoke with angels daily"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 22:6",verse:"Come now therefore, I pray thee, curse me this people; for they are too mighty for me: peradventure I shall prevail, that we may smite them, and that I may drive them out of the land: for I wot that he whom thou blessest is blessed, and he whom thou cursest is cursed.", insight:"Men traded on Balaam's name; a reputation for power is a dangerous currency."},
{q:"What did Balak's messengers carry to Balaam?", options:["The rewards of divination in their hand","A treaty of peace","The tribute of Moab","A golden calf"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 22:7",verse:"And the elders of Moab and the elders of Midian departed with the rewards of divination in their hand; and they came unto Balaam, and spake unto him the words of Balak.", insight:"Rewards of divination in hand; money was the first word in Balak's message."},
{q:"What did Balaam tell the messengers to do?", options:["Lodge here this night, and I will bring you word again, as the LORD shall speak unto me","Return at once to Balak","Go and curse Israel yourselves","Wait at the border seven days"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 22:8",verse:"And he said unto them, Lodge here this night, and I will bring you word again, as the LORD shall speak unto me: and the princes of Moab abode with Balaam.", insight:"Balaam at least asked the LORD first; the habit of asking is good, even in a divided heart."},
{q:"What was God's first answer to Balaam?", options:["Thou shalt not go with them; thou shalt not curse the people: for they are blessed","Go, but speak only blessing","Curse them, for they have sinned","Wait until the morning"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 22:12",verse:"And God said unto Balaam, Thou shalt not go with them; thou shalt not curse the people: for they are blessed.", insight:"'For they are blessed'; no curse can land where God has spoken blessing."},
{q:"What did Balaam tell Balak's princes in the morning?", options:["The LORD refuseth to give me leave to go with you","God has cursed Israel already","The journey is too long for me","Balak must come himself"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 22:13",verse:"And Balaam rose up in the morning, and said unto the princes of Balak, Get you into your land: for the LORD refuseth to give me leave to go with you.", insight:"He reported God's refusal honestly, this once; truth told plainly is its own defense."},
{q:"What did Balak do after the first refusal?", options:["Sent yet again princes, more, and more honourable than they","Gave up and made peace","Sent an army against Pethor","Cursed Balaam himself"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 22:15",verse:"And Balak sent yet again princes, more, and more honourable than they.", insight:"More princes, more honourable; temptation returns with a bigger offer when the first one fails."},
{q:"What did Balak promise Balaam?", options:["I will promote thee unto very great honour","The throne of Moab","Half of the land of the Amorites","A house in Shittim"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 22:17",verse:"For I will promote thee unto very great honour, and I will do whatsoever thou sayest unto me: come therefore, I pray thee, curse me this people.", insight:"'Very great honour'; the world bids high for a conscience it can rent."},
{q:"What did Balaam say about Balak's riches?", options:["If Balak would give me his house full of silver and gold, I cannot go beyond the word of the LORD","He would take the gold and flee","He demanded double the amount","He asked for the land instead"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 22:18",verse:"And Balaam answered and said unto the servants of Balak, If Balak would give me his house full of silver and gold, I cannot go beyond the word of the LORD my God, to do less or more.", insight:"A house full of silver and gold could not buy him; even Balaam knew some lines cannot be crossed."},
{q:"What did Balaam ask the second embassy to do?", options:["Tarry ye also here this night, that I may know what the LORD will say unto me more","Leave at once in the morning","Bring more gold","Go home to Balak"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 22:19",verse:"Now therefore, I pray you, tarry ye also here this night, that I may know what the LORD will say unto me more.", insight:"'What the LORD will say unto me more'; asking twice can mean hoping for a different answer."},
{q:"What permission did God give Balaam that night?", options:["Rise up, and go with them; but the word which I shall say unto thee, that shalt thou do","Go, and curse them freely","Stay, and do nothing","Go, and do as Balak bids"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 22:20",verse:"And God came unto Balaam at night, and said unto him, If the men come to call thee, rise up, and go with them; but yet the word which I shall say unto thee, that shalt thou do.", insight:"Go, but speak only My word; God sometimes lets a man walk the road his heart has chosen, on a leash."},
{q:"Why was God's anger kindled against Balaam?", options:["Because he went","Because he prayed","Because he refused Balak","Because he blessed Israel"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 22:22",verse:"And God’s anger was kindled because he went: and the angel of the LORD stood in the way for an adversary against him. Now he was riding upon his ass, and his two servants were with him.", insight:"His anger was kindled because he went; a willing heart toward sin angers God even when permission was granted."},
{q:"What did the donkey see that Balaam could not?", options:["The angel of the LORD standing in the way, with his sword drawn","A wall of fire","The camp of Israel","A pit in the road"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 22:23",verse:"And the ass saw the angel of the LORD standing in the way, and his sword drawn in his hand: and the ass turned aside out of the way, and went into the field: and Balaam smote the ass, to turn her into the way.", insight:"The beast saw the angel while the prophet was blind; God sometimes shows more to the humble than to the hireling."},
{q:"What happened at the narrow wall?", options:["The ass thrust herself unto the wall, and crushed Balaam's foot against the wall","The wall fell upon the ass","Balaam's sword broke in two","The angel struck Balaam down"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 22:25",verse:"And when the ass saw the angel of the LORD, she thrust herself unto the wall, and crushed Balaam’s foot against the wall: and he smote her again.", insight:"A crushed foot for a stubborn prophet; God hedges the way of those rushing toward sin."},
{q:"What did the donkey ask Balaam?", options:["What have I done unto thee, that thou hast smitten me these three times?","Why wilt thou not turn back?","Where is the angel thou canst not see?","Who opened my mouth?"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 22:28",verse:"And the LORD opened the mouth of the ass, and she said unto Balaam, What have I done unto thee, that thou hast smitten me these three times?", insight:"Three smitings, one question; even a beast can rebuke a prophet who beats the warning away."},
{q:"What command did the angel give Balaam?", options:["Go with the men: but only the word that I shall speak unto thee, that thou shalt speak","Turn back to Pethor at once","Curse Israel as Balak asked","Dismount and worship"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 22:35",verse:"And the angel of the LORD said unto Balaam, Go with the men: but only the word that I shall speak unto thee, that thou shalt speak. So Balaam went with the princes of Balak.", insight:"Go, but speak only My word; the errand was permitted, but the mouth was consecrated."}
]},
{n:23, name:"Balaam's First Oracles", seal:{ref:"Numbers 23:19",verse:"God is not a man, that he should lie; neither the son of man, that he should repent: hath he said, and shall he not do it? or hath he spoken, and shall he not make it good?"}, facts:["Did you know Samuel echoed this oracle when Saul fell, saying, \"The Strength of Israel will not lie nor repent\" (1 Samuel 15:29)?","Did you know Balaam built seven altars and offered seven bullocks and seven rams at each of two stations, and God answered both times with blessing instead of curses?","Did you know Balaam's wish, \"Let me die the death of the righteous,\" went unanswered: he died by the sword in Israel's war with Midian (Numbers 31:8)?"], questions:[
{q:"How many altars did Balaam order Balak to build?", options:["Seven altars","Three altars","Twelve altars","One altar"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 23:1",verse:"And Balaam said unto Balak, Build me here seven altars, and prepare me here seven oxen and seven rams.", insight:"Seven altars for a hired curse; God can take the machinery of divination and fill it with blessing."},
{q:"What did Balak and Balaam offer on every altar?", options:["A bullock and a ram","A lamb and a dove","Fine flour and oil","Two turtledoves"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 23:2",verse:"And Balak did as Balaam had spoken; and Balak and Balaam offered on every altar a bullock and a ram.", insight:"Bullock and ram on every altar; lavish sacrifice cannot buy a word God has not spoken."},
{q:"What did Balaam tell Balak to do while he went aside?", options:["Stand by thy burnt offering, and I will go","Return to his tent","Offer a second sacrifice","Call the princes together"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 23:3",verse:"And Balaam said unto Balak, Stand by thy burnt offering, and I will go: peradventure the LORD will come to meet me: and whatsoever he sheweth me I will tell thee. And he went to an high place.", insight:"'Stand by thy burnt offering'; even Balak had to wait on the LORD's answer."},
{q:"Whom did Balaam meet when he went to the high place?", options:["God met Balaam","An angel barred his way","The elders of Midian","A whirlwind from the north"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 23:4",verse:"And God met Balaam: and he said unto him, I have prepared seven altars, and I have offered upon every altar a bullock and a ram.", insight:"God met Balaam; the God of Israel will meet even a hireling to defend His own."},
{q:"From where had Balak fetched Balaam?", options:["From Aram, out of the mountains of the east","From Egypt, out of the house of bondage","From Canaan, out of Hebron","From Edom, out of Seir"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 23:7",verse:"And he took up his parable, and said, Balak the king of Moab hath brought me from Aram, out of the mountains of the east, saying, Come, curse me Jacob, and come, defy Israel.", insight:"From Aram, out of the mountains of the east; a long journey to speak words that were never his."},
{q:"How did Balaam open his first oracle?", options:["How shall I curse, whom God hath not cursed? or how shall I defy, whom the LORD hath not defied?","Cursed be Jacob forevermore","Let Moab rejoice in victory","Hear me, O Balak, and tremble"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 23:8",verse:"How shall I curse, whom God hath not cursed? or how shall I defy, whom the LORD hath not defied?", insight:"'How shall I curse, whom God hath not cursed?'; the first oracle is the whole book in one question."},
{q:"How did Balaam describe Israel?", options:["The people shall dwell alone, and shall not be reckoned among the nations","A people scattered to the winds","A nation like all the nations","A tribe without a land"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 23:9",verse:"For from the top of the rocks I see him, and from the hills I behold him: lo, the people shall dwell alone, and shall not be reckoned among the nations.", insight:"Dwelling alone, not reckoned among the nations; God's people are set apart, not lost in the crowd."},
{q:"What did Balaam say about numbering Jacob?", options:["Who can count the dust of Jacob, and the number of the fourth part of Israel?","They are fewer than the stars","They can be counted in one day","Their number is seventy souls"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 23:10",verse:"Who can count the dust of Jacob, and the number of the fourth part of Israel? Let me die the death of the righteous, and let my last end be like his!", insight:"Who can count the dust of Jacob? God's promise to multiply is beyond all reckoning."},
{q:"What did Balaam wish for himself?", options:["Let me die the death of the righteous, and let my last end be like his","Let me live forever in Moab","Let me see Balak's victory","Let me return to Pethor in honour"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 23:10",verse:"Who can count the dust of Jacob, and the number of the fourth part of Israel? Let me die the death of the righteous, and let my last end be like his!", insight:"He wished a righteous death while selling his voice to unrighteousness; wishing is not the same as turning."},
{q:"How did Balak react to the first oracle?", options:["What hast thou done unto me? I took thee to curse mine enemies, and thou hast blessed them altogether","He rejoiced and paid Balaam double","He wept and repented","He built seven more altars"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 23:11",verse:"And Balak said unto Balaam, What hast thou done unto me? I took thee to curse mine enemies, and, behold, thou hast blessed them altogether.", insight:"'Thou hast blessed them altogether'; Balak's complaint is the testimony of God's faithfulness."},
{q:"How did Balaam answer Balak's anger?", options:["Must I not take heed to speak that which the LORD hath put in my mouth?","I will curse them next time","The omens were unclear","Balak's altars were too few"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 23:12",verse:"And he answered and said, Must I not take heed to speak that which the LORD hath put in my mouth?", insight:"Must I not speak what the LORD put in my mouth? The hired mouth was mastered by a higher Word."},
{q:"What was Balak's plan at the second place?", options:["Thou shalt see but the utmost part of them, and shalt not see them all: and curse me them from thence","Balaam should see all of Israel at once","They would wait until nightfall","Balaam should fast seven days"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 23:13",verse:"And Balak said unto him, Come, I pray thee, with me unto another place, from whence thou mayest see them: thou shalt see but the utmost part of them, and shalt not see them all: and curse me them from thence.", insight:"See only part of them, Balak hoped; but God does not shrink when you narrow your view."},
{q:"Where did Balak bring Balaam for the second oracle?", options:["Into the field of Zophim, to the top of Pisgah","To the plains of Jericho","To the top of mount Hor","To the valley of Shittim"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 23:14",verse:"And he brought him into the field of Zophim, to the top of Pisgah, and built seven altars, and offered a bullock and a ram on every altar.", insight:"The field of Zophim, the watchers' field; Balak watched for a curse and saw only blessing."},
{q:"How did the second oracle begin?", options:["Rise up, Balak, and hear; hearken unto me, thou son of Zippor","Sleep, Balak, and dream","Flee, Balak, for thy life","Be silent, Balak, and listen"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 23:18",verse:"And he took up his parable, and said, Rise up, Balak, and hear; hearken unto me, thou son of Zippor:", insight:"'Rise up, Balak, and hear'; God bids the proud stand up to receive the word they dread."},
{q:"What did Balaam declare about God?", options:["God is not a man, that he should lie; neither the son of man, that he should repent","God is as the gods of Moab","God changes as the moon changes","God forgets His promises"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 23:19",verse:"God is not a man, that he should lie; neither the son of man, that he should repent: hath he said, and shall he not do it? or hath he spoken, and shall he not make it good?", insight:"God is not a man, that He should lie; His promises are not moods, they are rock."},
{q:"What command had Balaam received?", options:["I have received commandment to bless: and he hath blessed; and I cannot reverse it","To curse Israel utterly","To sacrifice to Chemosh","To return to Aram at once"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 23:20",verse:"Behold, I have received commandment to bless: and he hath blessed; and I cannot reverse it.", insight:"'I cannot reverse it'; a blessing commanded by God is past all undoing."},
{q:"How did God look on Jacob's iniquity?", options:["He hath not beheld iniquity in Jacob, neither hath he seen perverseness in Israel","He counted every transgression","He remembered the golden calf","He saw only their rebellion"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 23:21",verse:"He hath not beheld iniquity in Jacob, neither hath he seen perverseness in Israel: the LORD his God is with him, and the shout of a king is among them.", insight:"He hath not beheld iniquity in Jacob; God sees His people through the covering of His own choosing."},
{q:"What did Balaam say was among Israel?", options:["The shout of a king is among them","The murmur of rebellion","The wailing of captives","The silence of fear"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 23:21",verse:"He hath not beheld iniquity in Jacob, neither hath he seen perverseness in Israel: the LORD his God is with him, and the shout of a king is among them.", insight:"The shout of a king among them; where God reigns, His people do not whisper."},
{q:"What did Balaam say brought Israel out of Egypt?", options:["God","Their own armies","The chariots of Pharaoh","The magicians of Egypt"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 23:22",verse:"God brought them out of Egypt; he hath as it were the strength of an unicorn.", insight:"God brought them out of Egypt; the Exodus has one Author, and Balaam named Him."},
{q:"What protection did Israel have against enchantment?", options:["Surely there is no enchantment against Jacob, neither is there any divination against Israel","The altars of Balak","The walls of their camp","The spears of their warriors"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 23:23",verse:"Surely there is no enchantment against Jacob, neither is there any divination against Israel: according to this time it shall be said of Jacob and of Israel, What hath God wrought!", insight:"No enchantment against Jacob; every spell breaks on the people God has blessed."}
]},
{n:24, name:"The Star Prophecy", seal:{ref:"Numbers 24:17",verse:"I shall see him, but not now: I shall behold him, but not nigh: there shall come a Star out of Jacob, and a Sceptre shall rise out of Israel, and shall smite the corners of Moab, and destroy all the children of Sheth."}, facts:["Did you know the wise men who came to Bethlehem said, \"We have seen his star in the east,\" echoing Balaam's star out of Jacob (Matthew 2:2)?","Did you know Balaam looked down on Israel \"abiding in his tents according to their tribes,\" and the sight moved even this hired prophet to cry, \"How goodly are thy tents, O Jacob\"?","Did you know that when Balak \"smote his hands together\" in anger, his whole curse-for-hire scheme collapsed before the God he could not buy (Numbers 24:10)?"], questions:[
{q:"What did Balaam not do before the third oracle?", options:["He went not, as at other times, to seek for enchantments","He built no altars at all","He refused to speak","He fled to the wilderness"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 24:1",verse:"And when Balaam saw that it pleased the LORD to bless Israel, he went not, as at other times, to seek for enchantments, but he set his face toward the wilderness.", insight:"No more enchantments sought; even Balaam learned that God's blessing needs no sorcery."},
{q:"What came upon Balaam when he saw Israel by tribes?", options:["The spirit of God came upon him","A deep sleep fell upon him","A whirlwind carried him away","The angel struck him blind"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 24:2",verse:"And Balaam lifted up his eyes, and he saw Israel abiding in his tents according to their tribes; and the spirit of God came upon him.", insight:"The Spirit of God came upon him; God can anoint a mouth He did not choose to honor the people He loves."},
{q:"How did Balaam describe himself?", options:["The man whose eyes are open","The servant of Balak","The prophet of Moab","The seer of the east"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 24:3",verse:"And he took up his parable, and said, Balaam the son of Beor hath said, and the man whose eyes are open hath said:", insight:"Eyes open at last; the hireling prophet finally saw what he was paid to curse."},
{q:"How did Balaam receive the vision?", options:["Falling into a trance, but having his eyes open","Sleeping through the night","Climbing the mountain alone","Reading the stars"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 24:4",verse:"He hath said, which heard the words of God, which saw the vision of the Almighty, falling into a trance, but having his eyes open:", insight:"Falling, yet with eyes open; God brings men low to lift their sight high."},
{q:"How did Balaam greet Israel's tents?", options:["How goodly are thy tents, O Jacob, and thy tabernacles, O Israel","How empty are thy tents, O Jacob","How scattered are thy camps","How fearful are thy hosts"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 24:5",verse:"How goodly are thy tents, O Jacob, and thy tabernacles, O Israel!", insight:"How goodly are thy tents; from the hills of Moab, Israel's camp looked like beauty itself."},
{q:"To what did Balaam liken Israel's tents?", options:["Valleys spread forth, as gardens by the river's side","Desert thorns in the wind","Smoke rising from a fire","Clouds without water"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 24:6",verse:"As the valleys are they spread forth, as gardens by the river’s side, as the trees of lign aloes which the LORD hath planted, and as cedar trees beside the waters.", insight:"Gardens by the river's side; God's people are planted, watered, and flourishing."},
{q:"What did Balaam say about Israel's king?", options:["His king shall be higher than Agag, and his kingdom shall be exalted","His king shall serve Balak","His kingdom shall fall to Moab","His king shall hide in the hills"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 24:7",verse:"He shall pour the water out of his buckets, and his seed shall be in many waters, and his king shall be higher than Agag, and his kingdom shall be exalted.", insight:"Higher than Agag, exalted; the kingdom Balaam saw coming would outlast every throne of Moab."},
{q:"What would Israel do to the nations his enemies?", options:["Eat up the nations, break their bones, and pierce them through with arrows","Make peace with them all","Pay tribute to them","Flee before them"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 24:8",verse:"God brought him forth out of Egypt; he hath as it were the strength of an unicorn: he shall eat up the nations his enemies, and shall break their bones, and pierce them through with his arrows.", insight:"Eat up the nations his enemies; the blessing carries a sword for those who fight God's people."},
{q:"To what animal did Balaam liken Israel?", options:["A lion: he couched, he lay down as a lion, and as a great lion","A lamb among wolves","An ox in the stall","A dove in the clefts"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 24:9",verse:"He couched, he lay down as a lion, and as a great lion: who shall stir him up? Blessed is he that blesseth thee, and cursed is he that curseth thee.", insight:"A lion couched; do not wake what God has settled into rest."},
{q:"What blessing-curse formula closed the third oracle?", options:["Blessed is he that blesseth thee, and cursed is he that curseth thee","Peace to all who seek peace","Woe to the enemies of Moab","Blessed are the peacemakers"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 24:9",verse:"He couched, he lay down as a lion, and as a great lion: who shall stir him up? Blessed is he that blesseth thee, and cursed is he that curseth thee.", insight:"Blessed the blesser, cursed the curser; God posted His own guard around His people."},
{q:"How did Balak show his anger?", options:["He smote his hands together","He tore his robe","He broke the altars","He wept aloud"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 24:10",verse:"And Balak’s anger was kindled against Balaam, and he smote his hands together: and Balak said unto Balaam, I called thee to curse mine enemies, and, behold, thou hast altogether blessed them these three times.", insight:"He smote his hands together; rage is the sound a failed scheme makes."},
{q:"How many times had Balaam blessed Israel, by Balak's own count?", options:["Three times","Once","Seven times","Never"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 24:10",verse:"And Balak’s anger was kindled against Balaam, and he smote his hands together: and Balak said unto Balaam, I called thee to curse mine enemies, and, behold, thou hast altogether blessed them these three times.", insight:"'Thou hast altogether blessed them these three times'; even the enemy keeps count of God's faithfulness."},
{q:"What did Balak tell Balaam to do?", options:["Flee thou to thy place","Stay and curse them once more","Offer again on Pisgah","Bring more princes"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 24:11",verse:"Therefore now flee thou to thy place: I thought to promote thee unto great honour; but, lo, the LORD hath kept thee back from honour.", insight:"'Flee thou to thy place'; the world dismisses the voice it cannot use."},
{q:"What did Balaam promise to tell Balak?", options:["What this people shall do to thy people in the latter days","The secrets of Egypt","The number of Israel's warriors","The way to appease the LORD"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 24:14",verse:"And now, behold, I go unto my people: come therefore, and I will advertise thee what this people shall do to thy people in the latter days.", insight:"What Israel would do in the latter days; the last oracle looks past Balak to the end of days."},
{q:"Whose knowledge did Balaam claim?", options:["The knowledge of the most High","The wisdom of the east","The secrets of the magicians","The counsel of Balak"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 24:16",verse:"He hath said, which heard the words of God, and knew the knowledge of the most High, which saw the vision of the Almighty, falling into a trance, but having his eyes open:", insight:"Knowledge of the most High; the prophet for hire ended up preaching the true God."},
{q:"What did Balaam say would come out of Jacob and Israel?", options:["A Star out of Jacob, and a Sceptre shall rise out of Israel","A flood out of Jacob","A famine out of Israel","A sword out of Jacob"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 24:17",verse:"I shall see him, but not now: I shall behold him, but not nigh: there shall come a Star out of Jacob, and a Sceptre shall rise out of Israel, and shall smite the corners of Moab, and destroy all the children of Sheth.", insight:"A Star out of Jacob, a Sceptre out of Israel; a King was coming, and even Moab's prophet saw Him."},
{q:"What would the ruler coming out of Jacob do?", options:["Have dominion, and destroy him that remaineth of the city","Spare the city and bless it","Flee from the city in fear","Pay tribute to the city"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 24:19",verse:"Out of Jacob shall come he that shall have dominion, and shall destroy him that remaineth of the city.", insight:"Out of Jacob comes dominion; the coming King does not merely visit, He reigns."},
{q:"What would become of Edom?", options:["Edom shall be a possession, Seir also shall be a possession for his enemies","Edom shall rule forever","Edom shall be forgotten","Edom shall join Israel"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 24:18",verse:"And Edom shall be a possession, Seir also shall be a possession for his enemies; and Israel shall do valiantly.", insight:"Edom a possession; the proud neighbor who barred the way would one day be inherited."},
{q:"What did Balaam say of Amalek?", options:["Amalek was the first of the nations; but his latter end shall be that he perish for ever","Amalek shall endure forever","Amalek shall lead the nations","Amalek shall repent and live"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 24:20",verse:"And when he looked on Amalek, he took up his parable, and said, Amalek was the first of the nations; but his latter end shall be that he perish for ever.", insight:"First of the nations, last in ruin; pride of place is no shelter from the end."},
{q:"From where would ships come in Balaam's last oracle?", options:["From the coast of Chittim","From the Red sea","From the river of Egypt","From the isles of Tarshish"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 24:24",verse:"And ships shall come from the coast of Chittim, and shall afflict Asshur, and shall afflict Eber, and he also shall perish for ever.", insight:"Ships from Chittim would afflict Asshur; God raises distant powers to humble the proud."}
]},
{n:25, name:"Phinehas' Zeal", seal:{ref:"Numbers 25:12",verse:"Wherefore say, Behold, I give unto him my covenant of peace:"}, facts:["Did you know twenty-four thousand died in the plague at Baal-peor, the largest death toll named in any single judgment of the wilderness years?","Did you know Phinehas is named a hero of the faith in Psalm 106, where his act \"was counted unto him for righteousness unto all generations for evermore\" (Psalm 106:30-31)?","Did you know Zimri and Cozbi's deaths ended the plague at once, and God credited Phinehas with making atonement for all Israel?"], questions:[
{q:"Where was Israel when the people began to sin with the daughters of Moab?", options:["In Shittim","In the plains of Jericho","At mount Hor","In the wilderness of Zin"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 25:1",verse:"And Israel abode in Shittim, and the people began to commit whoredom with the daughters of Moab.", insight:"Abiding in Shittim, they began to commit whoredom; sin starts while we are settled and at ease."},
{q:"What did the daughters of Moab call Israel to do?", options:["Unto the sacrifices of their gods: and the people did eat, and bowed down to their gods","To build them houses","To trade in the markets","To learn their songs"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 25:2",verse:"And they called the people unto the sacrifices of their gods: and the people did eat, and bowed down to their gods.", insight:"They ate, and bowed down; idolatry enters through the table before it reaches the altar."},
{q:"To whom did Israel join himself?", options:["Baal-peor","Chemosh","Baal-berith","Ashtaroth"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 25:3",verse:"And Israel joined himself unto Baal-peor: and the anger of the LORD was kindled against Israel.", insight:"Joined unto Baal-peor; what Balaam could not curse, Israel cursed by its own compromise."},
{q:"Whom was Moses commanded to take?", options:["All the heads of the people","The sons of Aaron","The elders of Midian","The princes of Moab"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 25:4",verse:"And the LORD said unto Moses, Take all the heads of the people, and hang them up before the LORD against the sun, that the fierce anger of the LORD may be turned away from Israel.", insight:"Take all the heads of the people; judgment begins with the leaders, for they led the sin."},
{q:"What judgment did the LORD command upon them?", options:["Hang them up before the LORD against the sun","Stone them at the camp gate","Burn them with fire","Drive them into the wilderness"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 25:4",verse:"And the LORD said unto Moses, Take all the heads of the people, and hang them up before the LORD against the sun, that the fierce anger of the LORD may be turned away from Israel.", insight:"Hung up against the sun; sin done in the open is judged in the open."},
{q:"What did Moses order the judges of Israel?", options:["Slay ye every one his men that were joined unto Baal-peor","Spare the princes","Flee from the camp","Offer a sacrifice"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 25:5",verse:"And Moses said unto the judges of Israel, Slay ye every one his men that were joined unto Baal-peor.", insight:"Slay every one joined to Baal-peor; half measures never purge a plague."},
{q:"What brazen act did an Israelite commit before all?", options:["Brought a Midianitish woman unto his brethren in the sight of Moses, and of all the congregation","Stole the golden vessels","Cursed the name of the LORD","Fled to the tents of Moab"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 25:6",verse:"And, behold, one of the children of Israel came and brought unto his brethren a Midianitish woman in the sight of Moses, and in the sight of all the congregation of the children of Israel, who were weeping before the door of the tabernacle of the congregation.", insight:"In the sight of Moses, while the congregation wept; sin at its boldest parades before grieving saints."},
{q:"Who rose up with a javelin in his hand?", options:["Phinehas, the son of Eleazar, the son of Aaron the priest","Moses the servant of the LORD","Joshua the son of Nun","Caleb the son of Jephunneh"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 25:7",verse:"And when Phinehas, the son of Eleazar, the son of Aaron the priest, saw it, he rose up from among the congregation, and took a javelin in his hand;", insight:"Phinehas rose up from among the congregation; one zealous man can turn the tide for a nation."},
{q:"What did Phinehas do in the tent?", options:["Thrust both of them through, the man of Israel, and the woman through her belly","Bound them and brought them out","Set the tent on fire","Called the judges to witness"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 25:8",verse:"And he went after the man of Israel into the tent, and thrust both of them through, the man of Israel, and the woman through her belly. So the plague was stayed from the children of Israel.", insight:"He thrust them both through; zeal for God's honor does not wait for a committee."},
{q:"What stopped the plague?", options:["Phinehas' act: so the plague was stayed from the children of Israel","Moses' prayer alone","The sacrifices of the people","The departure from Shittim"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 25:8",verse:"And he went after the man of Israel into the tent, and thrust both of them through, the man of Israel, and the woman through her belly. So the plague was stayed from the children of Israel.", insight:"The plague was stayed; righteous action in a corrupt hour can stop a judgment."},
{q:"How many died in the plague?", options:["Twenty and four thousand","Three thousand","Fourteen thousand","Seventy"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 25:9",verse:"And those that died in the plague were twenty and four thousand.", insight:"Twenty-four thousand dead; compromise with idols carries a body count."},
{q:"Why was God's wrath turned away from Israel?", options:["Phinehas was zealous for God's sake among them","Israel repented at once","Moses interceded all night","The Midianites fled"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 25:11",verse:"Phinehas, the son of Eleazar, the son of Aaron the priest, hath turned my wrath away from the children of Israel, while he was zealous for my sake among them, that I consumed not the children of Israel in my jealousy.", insight:"Zealous for God's sake; God honors the man who takes His honor personally."},
{q:"What did Phinehas' zeal prevent?", options:["God consuming the children of Israel in His jealousy","The Amorites attacking","The well drying up","The cloud departing"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 25:11",verse:"Phinehas, the son of Eleazar, the son of Aaron the priest, hath turned my wrath away from the children of Israel, while he was zealous for my sake among them, that I consumed not the children of Israel in my jealousy.", insight:"Lest He consume them in His jealousy; one man's zeal stood between a nation and wrath."},
{q:"What covenant did God give Phinehas?", options:["My covenant of peace","A covenant of war","A covenant of riches","A covenant of long life"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 25:12",verse:"Wherefore say, Behold, I give unto him my covenant of peace:", insight:"A covenant of peace to the man of the javelin; God's peace rests on those who contend for Him."},
{q:"What priesthood was promised to Phinehas and his seed?", options:["The covenant of an everlasting priesthood","A priesthood for forty years","The high priesthood for one generation","A priesthood in Shiloh only"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 25:13",verse:"And he shall have it, and his seed after him, even the covenant of an everlasting priesthood; because he was zealous for his God, and made an atonement for the children of Israel.", insight:"An everlasting priesthood; zeal for God echoes in generations not yet born."},
{q:"Why did Phinehas receive the everlasting priesthood?", options:["Because he was zealous for his God, and made an atonement for the children of Israel","Because he was the eldest son","Because Moses appointed him","Because the people chose him"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 25:13",verse:"And he shall have it, and his seed after him, even the covenant of an everlasting priesthood; because he was zealous for his God, and made an atonement for the children of Israel.", insight:"He made atonement for Israel; the zealot became the intercessor."},
{q:"Who was the slain Israelite?", options:["Zimri, the son of Salu, a prince of a chief house among the Simeonites","Korah the son of Izhar","Dathan the son of Eliab","On the son of Peleth"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 25:14",verse:"Now the name of the Israelite that was slain, even that was slain with the Midianitish woman, was Zimri, the son of Salu, a prince of a chief house among the Simeonites.", insight:"Zimri, a prince among the Simeonites; rank did not shield him from judgment."},
{q:"Who was the slain Midianite woman?", options:["Cozbi, the daughter of Zur, head over a people, of a chief house in Midian","The daughter of Balak","A handmaid of the tabernacle","The wife of Zimri of Judah"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 25:15",verse:"And the name of the Midianitish woman that was slain was Cozbi, the daughter of Zur; he was head over a people, and of a chief house in Midian.", insight:"Cozbi, daughter of a chief house; the snare was set by royalty, and royalty fell with it."},
{q:"What did the LORD command against the Midianites?", options:["Vex the Midianites, and smite them","Make peace with the Midianites","Ignore the Midianites","Trade with the Midianites"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 25:17",verse:"Vex the Midianites, and smite them:", insight:"Vex them, and smite them; those who seduce God's people into sin become His enemies."},
{q:"Why were the Midianites to be smitten?", options:["They vexed Israel with their wiles, beguiling them in the matter of Peor, and in the matter of Cozbi","They stole Israel's cattle","They blocked the king's highway","They allied with the Amorites"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 25:18",verse:"For they vex you with their wiles, wherewith they have beguiled you in the matter of Peor, and in the matter of Cozbi, the daughter of a prince of Midian, their sister, which was slain in the day of the plague for Peor’s sake.", insight:"Beguiled in the matter of Peor and of Cozbi; God names the seduction when He names the sentence."}
]}
]);
